This slice removes two independent sources of false-negative physical Self Update evidence:

- release discovery may receive the workflow's read-only `github.token` for GitHub API list/tag calls;
- the token is validated, bounded, and never sent to immutable release asset URLs;
- Windows process observation completes the parameterless `WaitForExit()` drain and refreshes process state before reading `ExitCode`;
- falsification tests reject CR/LF token injection before any network effect and enforce the API/asset credential boundary;
- a static physical-runner contract binds the token to exactly one least-privilege workflow step and preserves `contents: read`.

