Goal: turn explicit DevOS Session / Surface presentation intent into an exact main-process Browser activation without making Browser tab selection a Session-focus authority.

Implemented on this branch:
- pure zero-authority Session/Surface activation descriptor layered on the existing exact `planDevOSSessionFocus` / `planDevOSSurfaceFocus` planners;
- fail-closed runtime executor with dependency injection and no hidden retry;
- exact main-process Browser activation through the existing `registry.select -> attachSelected -> invalidatePerception` path;
- physical Browser activation happens before presentation-focus commit; activation failure leaves focus unchanged;
- ambiguous multi-Browser Session intent commits Session-only focus and requires explicit Surface selection;
- Session with no Browser remains session-only;
- valid stored Browser preference may guide exact Session navigation but never becomes Surface-selection authority;
- sender-validated narrow presentation-focus IPC remains separate from generic `SELECT_TAB`;
- falsification/static contracts cover ambiguity, dead/missing targets, authority-bearing inputs, no URL/title guessing, no second scheduler/polling loop, and Browser-selection independence.

Invariants:
- Session remains the primary object; Browser remains a Surface;
- no URL/title guessing and no cross-Session fallback;
- Browser `SELECT_TAB` never creates or rewrites DevOS presentation focus;
- main process owns physical WebContents selection;
- renderer gets no selection/routing/scheduler/execution/effect authority;
- sender validation and narrow preload IPC are preserved;
- canonical integration authority is not advanced by this PR.

